// A handler arm performing an op of the effect it handles asks an OUTER
// install to serve it (an arm's performs resolve outer, never self — the
// arm runs in the install's own world). With one install there is no outer
// handler: the row re-adds E through row(h) at the tee, E reaches the root,
// and the executable refuses. The boot accepted it (installed-somewhere) and
// the program aborted inside the arm.
effect E { op() -> Int, twice() -> Int }
handler h { op() => resume(10), twice() => resume(op() + op()) }
fn main() = (twice()) ~> h
